# Integer64 narrowing assignment rejected

Verifies assigning a bigint value to an int64 variable is rejected at compile
time through the complete CLI pipeline. The language defines no implicit
narrowing conversion, so the assignment fails instead of silently truncating
a value that may not fit.

>>> source
wide: bigint = 170141183460469231731687303715884105728
narrow: int64 = wide
print(narrow)

<<< stdout

<<< stderr
eck: type mismatch: variable `narrow` expects `int64`, expression produces `bigint` at Span { start: 71, end: 75 }

<<< exit
1
